      "writtenOn": "2018-12-21T21:29:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if the resetting task owns a mutex?  What happens if the resetting task is waiting on a mutex and then the current mutex owner releases the mutex?  Can you write some test tasks to verify behavior for this?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 514,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 514,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e33610a741d6fccee39d7689b06355d534bbc14e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1d7ea1d_98a67060",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/task.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 514,
      "author": {
        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-24T20:29:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep good question. I\u0027ve just shared a doc with you where there was some discussion of this. \n\nThe conclusion was that a task that supports reset is responsible for releasing any mutexes it was holding [when it was reset] during the cleanup stage at task startup [after reset].\n\nTo enable this, I have a follow up CL ready which updates the implementation of mutex to store the task id rather than a constant value of 2, as the lock. It also adds a \u0027try_unlock\u0027 function that allows the task to release mutexes only if it was the task holding them.\n\nThe author of the task must ensure that it attempts to release all mutexes that *could* have been held (as well as performing any additional cleanup required).\n\nIf the task being reset is waiting on a mutex, and it is released before the reset is done, I believe that\u0027s fine, and will not affect / be affected by the reset. \n\nThe final part is that the reset should remove the task being reset from the waiters of all mutexes, so as to not be notified when it is released. This involves being able to iterate through all the mutexes (also discussed in the doc), which I think should also come in a follow up change.",
      "parentUuid": "a6ac99f1_07ac6a2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 514,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 514,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "e33610a741d6fccee39d7689b06355d534bbc14e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
