      "writtenOn": "2018-12-24T20:29:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. We can easily just return if resets are unsupported, but this doesn\u0027t seem ideal as it could hide programming errors. Since we are *only* trying to catch programming errors here, I think I\u0027d be more in favour of something more drastic like an assert (and crash), but only in dev mode. Or a combination of both, to catch things early, and not break in production if we somehow get there by accident anyway. WDYT?",
