    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c7c4338_cb1e5591",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/task.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 566,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-26T18:44:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d prefer to not do asserts in the code, which reliability is critical for the overall system security. but I can live with it, if other cr50 folks feel that\u0027s acceptable.\n\nin any case, as of now, an accidental call of task_*_resets() in a task, which is not resettable, would lead to an unexpected behavior, which may be hard to catch. and, as we go forward, calling those functions may be introduced in such tasks through adding those calls to common utility functions, and then using utility functions in a non-resettable task - it can be hidden under several levels of func calls, so not immediately apparent that a particular function *can* under certain circumstances be called from a non-resettable task. \n\nso, I believe it should be fixed. the simplest fix imo is just ignoring these calls in non-resettable functions (feel free to add debug-only assert + CPRINT)",
